facts: values that winch reads from each host

Facts are values that winch reads from each host before the plan, such
as the OS release.

Reading a fact:
  Expressions read a fact as facts.os.id, and templates as {{
  facts.os.id }}. A host from hosts or match() has its facts too:
  match("backup")[0].facts.ssh.ed25519. Facts are a fixed set. A read of
  an unknown fact is an error.

    # winch.yaml
    name: demo
    hosts:
      web1.example.com: {}
    steps:
      - recipe: base
    recipes:
      base:
        require:
          - !expr facts.os.id == "debian" and facts.os.version == "13"
        steps:
          - reboot:
              if_required: true
            when: !expr facts.reboot_required

    # The plan fails a host that is not Debian 13. A host that needs a
    # reboot reboots.

When winch reads them:
  winch reads the facts once per host per run, before the first step,
  and again after a reboot. It also reads the facts of each other host
  that hosts and match() can reach. They describe the host before the
  run.

Keys:
  os               map      -  OS release of the host
  os.id            string   -  distribution, such as debian or ubuntu
  os.version       string   -  release number, such as 13 or 24.04
  os.codename      string   -  release code name, such as trixie or noble
  os.arch          string   -  CPU architecture: amd64 or arm64
  reboot_required  boolean  -  pending reboot
  ssh              map      -  public SSH host keys
  ssh.ed25519      string   -  Ed25519 host key, such as ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nz…
  ssh.ecdsa        string   -  ECDSA host key, such as ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 AAAAE2Vj…
  ssh.rsa          string   -  RSA host key, such as ssh-rsa AAAAB3Nz…
  net              map      -  addresses of the default routes
  net.ipv4         string   -  IPv4 address, such as 192.0.2.10
  net.ipv6         string   -  IPv6 address, such as 2001:db8::10

Run "winch doc facts.<key>" for the full text of a key.
